<urn:atm:triage:finding/AZS2-QA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AZS2-QA-002" ;
  triage:title "AC8's retained-1.5.14-binary proof is a simulated SQL test, not a real cross-binary fixture" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/tests/schema_version_compat.rs:41-70 -- AC8 requires 'a retained 1.5.14 binary can assign/ack/complete on the migrated database; the new binary then observes those writes.' The only test claiming this coverage self-discloses in its own comment that it intentionally does not link a second binary into this crate -- it performs direct v1-table SQL from the current binary instead. Note: the sprint doc's own Required Validation section never names a cross-binary fixture command; arch-qa/req-qa treated the underlying fact as informational only, consistent with established practice that cross-binary/cross-version integration proof belongs in the colima integration testbed, not a per-crate cargo test. Fix: either add a real cross-binary fixture at the colima integration-testbed layer, or formally narrow AC8's wording via sprint-doc amendment, with cross-binary proof tracked as a separate integration-testbed task." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/tests/schema_version_compat.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
